 ### [Image Transformation Methods](10425-image-transformation-methods.md)
-A forward projection method where volume data is transformed so rays can be projected into the volume and onto the image plane using a scan line method at any angle via Euler angle transformations.
+A feed-forward (projective) volume rendering technique where the volume data is transformed into an intermediate space aligned with the image plane, allowing standard 2D compositing or projection. Unlike image-order methods that trace rays through the volume, these methods enumerate voxels, apply a viewing transformation, and then project the result. They are distinguished from their siblings by their specific decomposition of the transformation into incremental beam and slice updates to exploit spatial coherency and parallelism.
 
